# RBM evidence and query-partition gap

New public design supplement to frozen RBM-GAP-007. Actual author: `/root/research_architect`, Dataset Research Architect, 2026-10-10 UTC. Status: prospective specification, not generated data or approval. The existing `kind=belief` contract remains unchanged. Factual witness definitions are in the new `schemas/BELIEF_CONTROL_PROPERTIES.md`.

## Measured reason for this pilot

The frozen actual expert analysis `reviews/expert/RBM-gap-analysis-20261010T015614Z.md/.json` recomputes the 24 current approved records and joins 72 existing receipts. It finds only three exact world tables and no useful query after two or more observations, no unobserved invariant with multiple survivors, no multiworld entailed-null, no active redundant nonempty step, no cross-fact contradiction and no post-empty observation. Current targets are correct. The discrimination gap is specific: each of two incomplete support-size/observed-fact heuristics matches all 72 query usefulness or entailment flags. This is corpus compatibility with a shortcut, not measured model behavior.

This design requires exact value-partition computation after conjunction, with equal-support controls making support size and observation membership insufficient. It does not add priors, weights, noise, authority, delays, actions, utility or a selected inspection. The broader original RBM curriculum remains a hypothesis roadmap; Bayes, inspection utility, calibration and memory composition do not follow from this pilot.

## Four fresh structural source families

Use source indices **12,13,18,19**, assigned before any variants: 12/13 train and 18/19 exposed dev under the common policy. Confirm the actual mapping. Do not use four contiguous train indices. The independent unit is the source family, including every context, name/ID/order view and probe. Four fresh world tables must be distinct from prior approved tables and from each other after order-invariant partition/incidence normalization; new names or magnitudes alone do not satisfy this requirement.

Use at least five actual visible fact roles: two distinct observation facts, an unobserved invariant query, an unobserved varying query, and an unoffered feature. One of the observed facts may be the third queried control, so the three queried roles plus two auxiliary roles suffice. Four roles suffice for the basic invariant/useful conjunction, but an all-three-queries-redundant context with both observation facts fixed needs an additional unoffered varying feature to keep survivor payloads genuinely different. Do not manufacture uncertainty by duplicating an identical complete payload under different world IDs. Prefer reused unoffered scalar values over a copied unique world-ID field.

The following profiles specify relationships, not concrete worlds or future targets. Let the two observation facts define a bipartite incidence graph: value blocks are vertices and an occupied joint cell is an edge weighted by the number of visible worlds in it. Ignore world/fact names and list order when comparing profiles. Each profile must support the full six-context requirements below.

| Source index / split | Distinct required profile |
|---|---|
| 12 / train | Crossed non-nested partitions with a cycle, uniform positive occupied-cell multiplicities, at least one unsupported individually possible conjunction, and asymmetric standalone observation support sizes. Equal-support selected cells have different queried-value partitions. Include the multiworld null/ambiguity/empty contrast in this family. |
| 13 / train | Connected acyclic incidence with a branching vertex of degree at least three, rather than the cyclic table. Both constraints are necessary for the unobserved invariant. Include active false/integer 0 separation in observation or final query partition evidence, and treat a literal `unknown` value as an ordinary scalar where supplied. |
| 18 / exposed dev | Cyclic incidence with nonuniform occupied-cell multiplicities, equal-cardinality selected supports of at least three worlds, and a distinguishing query with unequal positive value-bin counts. Include multiworld entailed-null and ambiguous-null controls; the differing weights/partitions distinguish it from the uniform cyclic profile. |
| 19 / exposed dev | A connected acyclic path incidence with maximum degree two, distinct from the branching profile. Active boolean/integer collisions affect exact filtering/partitioning: include true/integer 1 and false/integer 0 separators. Require the same equal-support, conjunction, contradiction and trace controls. |

Graph topology, weights and joint queried-value partitions must be checked from actual inputs. A profile name is not a witness. Require all four profiles to have different complete order-invariant signatures, and disclose any remaining shared submotifs. Mixed scalar types and null support should be available across train and dev; fact/world-ID style must not be tied to split. Proposed initial tables can have 8–20 distinct fact-payload worlds, but that range is a context-size bound, not a difficulty criterion or achieved count. Add states only to satisfy actual partition/control needs.

## Six supplied contexts per world table

Keep the same table and the same three base queried facts in every context. Queries are independent and concern the final filtered set. Rename/reorder them only through the declared schedule. Required properties are context-specific:

| Context | Exact design requirement |
|---|---|
| A: conjunctive partial evidence | Two observations on distinct facts each strictly reduce nonempty support. Final support contains at least two worlds with different complete payloads. An unobserved query is invariant, and removing either observation makes that same fact vary; another query remains distinguishing. The third query may be the directly observed control. |
| B: equal-support counterfactual | Change only one observation's typed equals value from A. Hold world table, ordered base queries, observation count and other observation fields fixed. Final support cardinality equals A and remains at least two, while the same distinguishing query changes usefulness. Require every offered query to be redundant here, with an unoffered fact still varying. |
| C: reordered evidence | Swap A's two observations. Final survivors/full query answers agree, but the actual ordered belief_sizes trace is recomputed and differs in at least one prefix cardinality. This requires unequal standalone support sizes; reordering is not a field-order renderer. |
| D: nonempty redundancy | Append to A an exact repeat of one earlier observation. Final survivors/full query answers agree, with a nonempty unchanged last prefix. The row itself witnesses the repeated nonempty step. |
| E: cross-fact contradiction | Change one observation equals value from A to a value supported individually in the same table. Both different-fact observations are individually possible, but their conjunction is empty. This is noiseless inconsistency, not uncertain authority or evidence arbitration. |
| F: absorption after empty | Append to E an ordinary observation that is individually satisfiable in the original table. The empty prefix remains empty, and the appended belief_sizes value is zero. Empty query counts/false flags are retained; no resurrection is allowed. |

These are constraints for later generation, not assigned answers for future records. If the selected table cannot satisfy all six controls and its structural profile, revise the table before review; do not weaken a claim after seeing a favorable target. The future oracle and reviewers must derive every survivor, prefix size, scalar bin, flag and guarantee independently.

Across supplied cases, require multiworld entailed-null, ambiguous query partitions containing null, and empty-belief null guarantees with distinct counts/flags; truthful tags belong only to rows containing the corresponding witnesses. At least one train family and one dev family should supply the complete null contrast. Active true/integer 1 and false/integer 0 controls must be demonstrated, not merely present in unused world cells. Typed equals counterfactuals outside the six actual contexts are audit probes unless explicitly supplied as corpus variants. Do not count probes as new contexts or records.

## Why 27 schedules replace the proposed nine

For role r in Z3, the original proposal uses i=r+u, p=r+v, n=r+u+v. Every role covers each marginal bucket three times and every pair bucket once, but the nuisance triple reveals r=i+p-n. Pooling observations over roles can look balanced while this deterministic role dependence remains. An independently executed mathematical review by `/root/research_architect/rbm_schedule_design` confirmed this.

Use independent shifts u,v,w in Z3: **i=r+u, p=r+v, n=r+w**. For each source/context/field order and each role, every one of 27 ID/position/fact-name triples occurs once, each marginal bucket 9 times and each pair bucket 3 times. All worlds, observations and queries receive the same consistent fact-name bijection. The two auxiliary facts stay distinct from the three queried roles and have equally styled arbitrary names; broader all-fact-role/world-ID independence is not implied.

The full schedule is the smallest uniform positive complete triple-support design. A modified nine-schedule option can put all roles on nine shared triple cells, but leaves 18 cells unsupported and retains a deterministic three-way relation. The accepted design choice is27, not an assertion that the original nine were invalid marginal/pair controls. Full arbitrary permutations would address row-level cyclic-order patterns at much greater correlated-record cost; they are not required or claimed here.

| Planned units | Count |
|---|---:|
| Source families / base contexts | 4 / 24 |
| Base context/query observations | 72 |
| Query/name/position schedules per context | 27 |
| Rotation-level tasks / query observations | 648 / 1,944 |
| Field-order renderings / rendered query observations | 1,296 / 3,888 |
| Planned train records / exposed dev records | 648 / 648 |

Counts are proposed. Verify actual unique tasks, name views and renderer pairs. Six contexts and 27 views remain correlated within four world tables; they do not add mechanism classes. The public filtering rule is still one deterministic mechanism.

## Required independent audits and honest difficulty

For every family/context/style, publish role and actual outcome histograms across all IDs, positions and fact names, and every pair/triple bucket. Include entailed/useful flags, empty/entailed/ambiguous audit categories, scalar types, full sorted count vectors, guaranteed-null interpretations, sorted final survivor-ID provenance and independently recomputed prefix survivor/count signatures. Those categories/provenance signatures are audit evidence; do not add new output fields. The full query payload comparison excludes only renamed query_id/fact-name identity. Every triple has each role once, so full outcome histograms must match across triples even when class frequencies are unequal. Aggregate only after validating each base context.

Measure observed-fact/support-size mutants and direct full-partition resolution separately. Each family must contain an actual A invariant that defeats both current incomplete heuristics, plus an A/B same-support usefulness change. Report exact typed targets and complete-task errors, rather than hiding a targeted rule failure in aggregate query accuracy. Audit current/prior exact world tables and order-invariant profiles, whole-family split custody, field-order pairs, supplied control pairs and actually executed probes. World-list/order-ID transformations require equivariant survivor sorting and exact prefix/query checks.

Supported difficulty is Level2 for consistent nuisance/renderer views and Level3 for decisive conjunctive filtering and typed/partition controls. E/F empty controls and D repetition may have simple substeps; give them honest component metrics. Larger support, longer lists and 27 schedules alone do not establish Levels4–7. Record world/fact/query/observation counts, strict nonempty support reductions, each invariant's essential constraint count, surviving payload distinctions, active typed separators, partition-bin counts/skew, contradiction's minimal witness size and steps after first empty. The two actual necessary constraints in A are more informative than raw observation count.

Generation, independently authored oracle, initial expert/red review and actual adjudication remain separate later executions. No prospective verdict author may supply private expected targets to a first reviewer. This public design is common input, not a review answer. Do not approve any batch before both final exact-hash reviews and formal evidence are complete. The design author's later adjudicator role must be disclosed; separate agents share an underlying model and can have correlated errors. Exposed dev and new structural profiles do not constitute sealed OOD or efficacy evidence.

